  §34.5 L9614: L,U = Δn(√p_g+√p_r)/(p_g−p_r) is the rationalised form of Δn/(√p_g−√p_r):
    identity holds on all 56 ordered pairs p ≤ 7, max |difference| = 8E-39
    sign: register 1309 prints (Δn)/(√pᵣ − √p_g) with Δn = nᵣ − n_g; the unit prints the
    same quotient with both differences reversed -- the same number (two sign flips).

  §34.5 L9619-L9620: (√(n−1) + √(n−4))/3 at n = 4..7, HALF_UP to the printed 7 dp:
    n=4  computed 0.5773503  printed 0.5773503  EXACT   (4 dp: 0.5774)
    n=5  computed 1.0000000  printed 1.0000000  EXACT   (4 dp: 1.0000)
    n=6  computed 1.2167605  printed 1.2168450  MISMATCH at 7 dp   (4 dp: 1.2168)
    n=7  computed 1.3938469  printed 1.3938270  MISMATCH at 7 dp   (4 dp: 1.3938)
    1/(√5−√2) = 1.2167605  (register 1322 calls it "1.2168"; register 1317 prints "1.2167")
    also (√(n−1)+√(n−4))/3 IS Δn/(√p_g−√p_r) for ns vs (n−1)d: p_g = n−1, p_r = n−4, Δn = 1, p_g−p_r = 3.

